Draw 4

Mentor × Escrow

This one gets weird.

Escrow:

hold(resource)
release_when(condition)

Mentor:

hold(knowledge)
release_when(student_ready)

Result:

Pedagogical Escrow

Knowledge_{available}
\neq
Knowledge_{released}

The mentor may possess an answer but withhold it until some state predicate becomes true.

if learner_can_integrate(lesson):
    release(lesson)
else:
    provide(next_trial)

Hound immediately catches the failure mode:

The mentor can falsely convince themselves the learner is “not ready” and hoard authority.

Mirror therefore adds:

withholding_requires(
    explicit_readiness_test,
    learner_interest,
    eventual_release_path
)

That transforms a story trope into a pedagogy/governance primitive.

