Draw 5

Tragic Flaw × Moral Hazard

These are almost twins.

Tragic flaw:

Trait\rightarrow repeated\ locally\ rational\ behavior
\rightarrow catastrophic\ global\ consequence

Moral hazard:

Protection\ from\ downside
\rightarrow changed\ incentives
\rightarrow excess\ risk

Combined:

A tragic flaw can be modeled as an internal incentive distortion.

def tragic_policy(agent, state):
    perceived_cost = true_cost * blindness_factor(agent)
    return maximize(reward - perceived_cost)

The character doesn’t have to be stupid.

Their internal payoff function is malformed.

That gives storytellers something much better than:

“He’s too proud.”

Instead:

Utility_{character}(status)
>
Utility_{character}(survival)

under certain states.

Now the tragedy becomes computational.

