Draw 6

Quest × Covenant

Quest:

Goal\rightarrow obstacles\rightarrow persistent\ pursuit

Covenant:

Unknown\ future\ states\rightarrow preserve(I)

Combined:

Quest = pursue(destination)

Covenant = preserve(direction)

That’s subtle.

A quest can fail if the original goal becomes impossible.

A covenant can survive because it regenerates appropriate behavior around an invariant.

So:

Quest tells you where to go. Covenant tells you what not to become while getting there.

That gives:

while not goal_reached:
    action = planner(goal, state)
    if violates_covenant(action):
        action = replan(action)
    execute(action)

Mirror likes this one because it turns the covenant into a planning constraint, rather than inspirational prose.

