What the daemons did in free play

There is a pattern.

Spider kept finding structural isomorphisms.

Hound repeatedly turned the analogy around and asked where it breaks.

Mirror tended to convert the interesting analogy into an invariant or admissibility constraint.

So the natural loop became:

Pair
\rightarrow Analogy
\rightarrow Structural\ invariant
\rightarrow Counterexample
\rightarrow Repair
\rightarrow New\ operator

That’s already a useful game.

But free play produces surprising primitives, not necessarily solutions.

So I tightened the leash.

