Another structured objective

Mission:

Teach someone a difficult skill without simply giving them the answer.

Spider draws:

Mentor + Escrow + Option

We already discovered pedagogical escrow.

Now structure it.

Lesson=L

release(L)\iff competence(state)\geq\theta

But learner also receives:

Option(request\_hint)

So:

while not solved(problem):
    observe(learner)
    if learner.requests_hint():
        release(minimum_useful_hint)
    elif learner_is_stuck_beyond_threshold():
        release(scaffold)
    else:
        preserve_search_space()

Hound tests:

* learner confidently heads the wrong direction,
* learner becomes frustrated,
* learner games the readiness metric.

Mirror adds the invariant:

Preserve productive agency, not difficulty itself.

That’s excellent.

Because suddenly the system knows why it is withholding information.

Not:

maximize(struggle)

but:

maximize(independent\ capability)

The narrative trope has improved the pedagogical deal.

