Now reverse it

This may be the most fertile part.

Don’t always use:

Narrative → Deal

Sometimes require:

Deal → Narrative.

Take insurance.

Ask the Narrative Gym:

What story trope has insurance topology?

Insurance:

many\ contribute\rightarrow rare\ sufferer\ receives\ concentrated\ aid

Narrative analogues appear:

* fellowship
* village
* sacrifice
* “all for one”
* guardian
* collective burden

So we discover:

Distributed Hero

Instead of:

Hero\ absorbs\ exceptional\ risk

we can write:

Group\ pools\ capacity
\rightarrow whoever\ encounters\ crisis\ temporarily\ becomes\ focal\ beneficiary

That’s a completely different story architecture.

