And options generate branching plots

Option:

right\ without\ obligation

Narratively:

Plant a capability early that the protagonist may—but need not—exercise later.

That’s essentially a better formulation of Chekhov’s Gun.

Normal version:

If the gun appears, it should fire.

Option version:

The gun establishes a future action branch.

AvailableActions_{t+1}
=
AvailableActions_t\cup\{fire\_gun\}

Whether it’s exercised becomes meaningful precisely because it could have been.

That’s more powerful than the conventional trope description.

